A bubble per area, sized by the value, over a map drawn in grey. Zurich calls this
a Signatur - the circle is the symbol carrying the number, and the areas underneath
are there to say where.

It reads the same value the choropleth would have coloured, so it takes no column
of its own. What it does take is the colour: an area's shade and a circle's size
would otherwise say the same thing twice, and the shades would fight the circles
for attention. So the base map goes grey, and its colour transition off with it,
since there is no longer a colour to transition.

The legend changes with it. A colour bar explains nothing about a map whose areas
are all the same grey, so the radius legend replaces it - the `legend` feature
draws whichever one this scalar names.

// #label Bubbles
// #hint A circle per area, sized by the value, over a grey map.

// #region magicNumbers
/** The radius in px of the largest bubble; the rest are scaled by area against it. */
const MAX_BUBBLE_RADIUS = 20;
// #endregion

// #region scales
// NOTE: A square-root scale, so that a value twice as large covers twice the area
// rather than twice the width, which is what a reader compares.
const radiusScale = d3.scaleSqrt().domain(state.valueDomain).range([0, MAX_BUBBLE_RADIUS]);
// #endregion

// #region overlays
const bubbleMap = sszvis
  .mapRendererBubble<Datum>()
  /* The first qualitative colour. An ordinal scale keyed by a name, as the examples key it. */
  .fill(sszvis.scaleQual6()("value"))
  .radius((d) => (sszvis.defined(d) && !Number.isNaN(d.value) ? radiusScale(d.value) : 0))
  .strokeWidth(sszvis.widthAdaptiveMapPathStroke(bounds.width));
// #endregion

// #region mapProps
.transitionColor(false)
// oxlint-disable-next-line anti-slop/no-shape-in-symbol-names -- the name of the sszvis method, not ours to pick.
.anchoredShape(bubbleMap)
// #endregion

// #scalar MAP_FILL () => sszvis.scaleGry()(0)
// #scalar LEGEND_COMPONENT sszvis.legendRadius().scale(radiusScale).tickFormat(sszvis.formatNumber)
/* The radius legend is about two of its largest circles wide, labels included, so that halves it. */
// #scalar LEGEND_X bounds.width / 2 - MAX_BUBBLE_RADIUS * 2
